From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anonymous <anonymous@localhost>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 02:05:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] WebUI: Expire unconfirmed sessions early and cap
 sessions

Under the authentication bypass (localhost or a whitelisted subnet), every
request without a session cookie started a new session, and each one kept its
API state for the whole session timeout: a client calling sync/maindata
without keeping cookies pinned a full snapshot (85-120 MB with ~9,000
torrents) per call, an easy way to exhaust memory.

A new session is now provisional until a request carries its cookie, and a
provisional session expires early. Making room for a new session evicts the
provisional session idle longest, or else the session idle longest, of the
same client address beyond the per-client limit and of all beyond the total
limit. Options (WebUI tab, WebAPI preferences, Preferences/WebUI/...):

- ProvisionalSessionTimeout / web_ui_provisional_session_timeout: 60 s
- MaxSessionsPerClient / web_ui_max_sessions_per_client: 8
- MaxSessions / web_ui_max_sessions: 32
